{
  "case_id": "2021-20-804",
  "document_hash": "f8277ad59f68b737bf930958828df1a0cb4cf5e6199b948dbd250425685b7a90",
  "records": [
    {
      "attribution": "Court Record",
      "case_id": "2021-20-804",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "f8277ad59f68b737bf930958828df1a0cb4cf5e6199b948dbd250425685b7a90",
      "evidence_id": "ev-f8277ad59f68-0000-0000",
      "kind": "procedural_event",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 2,
        "start": 2
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "APPEARANCES:\nRICHARD A. MORRIS, ESQUIRE, Houston, Texas; on behalf of the Petitioner.\nSOPAN JOSHI, Assistant to the Solicitor General, Department of Justice, Washington, D.C.; for the United States, as amicus curiae, supporting the Petitioner.\nMICHAEL B. KIMBERLY, ESQUIRE, Washington, D.C.; on behalf of the Respondent."
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Houston Community College System",
      "case_id": "2021-20-804",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "f8277ad59f68b737bf930958828df1a0cb4cf5e6199b948dbd250425685b7a90",
      "evidence_id": "ev-f8277ad59f68-0000-0001",
      "kind": "party_argument",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 4,
        "start": 4
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "The Fifth Circuit recognized a new cause of action based on an elected body censuring a member. That decision is wrong for two reasons. First, it ignores this country's history and parliamentary tradition, which recognize the right of elected bodies to govern their own affairs, including censuring members for violations of governance rules. And, second, it makes the Free Speech Clause into both a cudgel and a shield."
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Justice Thomas",
      "case_id": "2021-20-804",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "f8277ad59f68b737bf930958828df1a0cb4cf5e6199b948dbd250425685b7a90",
      "evidence_id": "ev-f8277ad59f68-0000-0002",
      "kind": "justice_question",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 6,
        "start": 6
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "JUSTICE THOMAS: Counsel, could a --a -- a legislative body -- is there any limit to its authority to expel or to sanction a member?"
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Justice Thomas",
      "case_id": "2021-20-804",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "f8277ad59f68b737bf930958828df1a0cb4cf5e6199b948dbd250425685b7a90",
      "evidence_id": "ev-f8277ad59f68-0001-0000",
      "kind": "justice_question",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 24,
        "start": 24
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "JUSTICE THOMAS: Is -- is there a historical basis for that? When we began our -- our argument -- when you began your argument, I asked you about the historical basis for sanctioning the member of the body. Is there a historical basis for sanctioning a private citizen?"
    },
    {
      "attribution": "United States (amicus curiae)",
      "case_id": "2021-20-804",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "f8277ad59f68b737bf930958828df1a0cb4cf5e6199b948dbd250425685b7a90",
      "evidence_id": "ev-f8277ad59f68-0001-0001",
      "kind": "amicus_argument",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 25,
        "start": 25
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "A censure resolution adopted by an elected body against one of its members does not abridge that member's freedom of speech."
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Court",
      "case_id": "2021-20-804",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "f8277ad59f68b737bf930958828df1a0cb4cf5e6199b948dbd250425685b7a90",
      "evidence_id": "ev-f8277ad59f68-0001-0005",
      "kind": "procedural_event",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 25,
        "start": 25
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "ORAL ARGUMENT OF SOPAN JOSHI FOR THE UNITED STATES, AS AMICUS CURIAE, SUPPORTING THE PETITIONER"
    },
    {
      "attribution": "United States (amicus curiae)",
      "case_id": "2021-20-804",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "f8277ad59f68b737bf930958828df1a0cb4cf5e6199b948dbd250425685b7a90",
      "evidence_id": "ev-f8277ad59f68-0001-0002",
      "kind": "amicus_argument",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 26,
        "start": 26
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "Elected bodies in our Anglo-American legal tradition have long entered disciplinary actions against their members, including for those members' speech, with no suggestion that it violated principles of free speech."
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Justice Thomas",
      "case_id": "2021-20-804",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "f8277ad59f68b737bf930958828df1a0cb4cf5e6199b948dbd250425685b7a90",
      "evidence_id": "ev-f8277ad59f68-0001-0004",
      "kind": "justice_question",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 40,
        "start": 40
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "JUSTICE THOMAS: It includes: \"Be it further resolved that the Respondent is hereby publicly censured for his conduct.\" That's -- you say we can resolve it on that. But the next paragraph in that censure resolution is: \"Be it further resolved that the Respondent is ineligible.\" And it goes on to -- to impose the other sanctions. On what basis do we disaggregate the resolution?"
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Michael B. Kimberly (respondent)",
      "case_id": "2021-20-804",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "f8277ad59f68b737bf930958828df1a0cb4cf5e6199b948dbd250425685b7a90",
      "evidence_id": "ev-f8277ad59f68-0001-0003",
      "kind": "party_argument",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 43,
        "start": 43
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "The question here boils down to whether the resolution of censure adopted by HCC's Board of Trustees was merely an expression of government opinion concerning the content of Mr. Wilson's speech or instead a punishment for it."
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Court",
      "case_id": "2021-20-804",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "f8277ad59f68b737bf930958828df1a0cb4cf5e6199b948dbd250425685b7a90",
      "evidence_id": "ev-f8277ad59f68-0001-0006",
      "kind": "procedural_event",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 43,
        "start": 43
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "ORAL ARGUMENT OF MICHAEL B. KIMBERLY ON BEHALF OF THE RESPONDENT"
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Justice Thomas",
      "case_id": "2021-20-804",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "f8277ad59f68b737bf930958828df1a0cb4cf5e6199b948dbd250425685b7a90",
      "evidence_id": "ev-f8277ad59f68-0002-0001",
      "kind": "justice_question",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 45,
        "start": 45
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "JUSTICE THOMAS: Petitioner seems to suggest that -- or argue that if we -- if the courts get involved in this, that we would be involved in the rough and tumble of politics and that it would not be productive. What would be your -- your response to that?"
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Justice Thomas",
      "case_id": "2021-20-804",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "f8277ad59f68b737bf930958828df1a0cb4cf5e6199b948dbd250425685b7a90",
      "evidence_id": "ev-f8277ad59f68-0002-0003",
      "kind": "justice_question",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 46,
        "start": 46
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "JUSTICE THOMAS: Now what is that?"
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Justice Kagan",
      "case_id": "2021-20-804",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "f8277ad59f68b737bf930958828df1a0cb4cf5e6199b948dbd250425685b7a90",
      "evidence_id": "ev-f8277ad59f68-0003-0000",
      "kind": "justice_question",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 64,
        "start": 64
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "JUSTICE KAGAN: Which side of your line does Senator McCarthy's censure fall on?"
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Board",
      "case_id": "2021-20-804",
      "confidence": 0.8,
      "document_hash": "f8277ad59f68b737bf930958828df1a0cb4cf5e6199b948dbd250425685b7a90",
      "evidence_id": "ev-f8277ad59f68-0004-0000",
      "kind": "party_argument",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 85,
        "start": 85
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "But the Board offers two interests here. It offers as interest to be able to speak in response to Mr. Wilson, who was no stranger to the hurly-burly of politics and who was publicly using a website to accuse his fellow trustees of crimes and violations of law without supporting evidence. But, if you tethered that to a rules violation, then that would violate the First Amendment."
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Chief Justice and Justice Thomas",
      "case_id": "2021-20-804",
      "confidence": 0.6,
      "document_hash": "f8277ad59f68b737bf930958828df1a0cb4cf5e6199b948dbd250425685b7a90",
      "evidence_id": "ev-f8277ad59f68-0004-0001",
      "kind": "justice_question",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 86,
        "start": 86
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "uncertain",
      "text": "As -- as to what will be the impact if this Court were to affirm the Fifth Circuit's ruling, to the Chief Justice's concern, it will spawn lawsuits, and courts will have to engage in reviewing the sausage makings of, to Justice Thomas's concern about resolutions, where things are not disaggregated."
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Court",
      "case_id": "2021-20-804",
      "confidence": 0.8,
      "document_hash": "f8277ad59f68b737bf930958828df1a0cb4cf5e6199b948dbd250425685b7a90",
      "evidence_id": "ev-f8277ad59f68-0004-0002",
      "kind": "fact",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 87,
        "start": 87
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "While it may be unusual in the U.S. Congress to censure, local bodies do it about once every other day in any given year, and they do it for all number of reasons, including for conduct that takes place outside the body."
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Chief Justice Roberts",
      "case_id": "2021-20-804",
      "confidence": 0.9,
      "document_hash": "f8277ad59f68b737bf930958828df1a0cb4cf5e6199b948dbd250425685b7a90",
      "evidence_id": "ev-f8277ad59f68-0004-0003",
      "kind": "justice_question",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 87,
        "start": 87
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "CHIEF JUSTICE ROBERTS: Thank you, counsel. The case is submitted."
    },
